  "notes": "Create binds mysql_indexes.compile_create (reviewed, observed native DDL); editing binds the index alter, which changes visibility and then the name (MySQL refuses both in one ALTER TABLE, error 1176). Key-part rows use the compiler's own keys. Round-tripped 2026-11-05 on the MySQL 9.7.0 demo (tools/tests/test_ui_descriptor_roundtrip_mysql.py): normal, fulltext (ngram parser) and spatial kinds, BTREE and HASH (MEMORY) methods, prefix, descending and expression key parts, comment, invisibility, secondary engine attribute, key block size (MyISAM), algorithm and lock, then a rename with a visibility change, each read back. MySQL refuses ALGORITHM=INPLACE with an expression key part (1846)."
